{
  "definitions": [
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 12,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "0a82089db438d6896e57def6a6d687fd829e250b2e3a57f86e1114728cabfd3d",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the N = 0 base case of binRel by equating the accumulated and output sequences; it is a mathematical-summary equation and does not replace program execution.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-0a82089db438d6896e57def6a6d687fd829e250b2e3a57f86e1114728cabfd3d",
      "start_line": 11,
      "text": "  rule binRel(N, ACC, OUT) => ACC ==K OUT\n    requires N ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 19,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "311c7818aa61ab48edceaaf524aa96cdc5343c25e35edeb7b7895c50438f7e39",
      "rationale": "This is the positive-N recursive equation defining binRel through quotient-by-two and a prepended remainder digit; it defines the loop summary rather than adding an independent fact or an execution rewrite.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-311c7818aa61ab48edceaaf524aa96cdc5343c25e35edeb7b7895c50438f7e39",
      "start_line": 14,
      "text": "  rule binRel(N, ACC, OUT)\n    => binRel(\n         (N -Int pyMod(N, 2)) /Int 2,\n         iCons(48 +Int pyMod(N, 2), ACC),\n         OUT)\n    requires N >Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 22,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "73d9b9e52c4141a668b87a1bda99e477853f9ac07bdde4e178dff6db56018487",
      "rationale": "This equation completes binRel's sign partition by defining the summary as false for negative N, providing a total definitional case without matching operational state.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-73d9b9e52c4141a668b87a1bda99e477853f9ac07bdde4e178dff6db56018487",
      "start_line": 21,
      "text": "  rule binRel(N, _ACC, _OUT) => false\n    requires N <Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 30,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "bb0dd8b44a02de305b300de162887fd197bafc6ab3bffe93bdff08e62e6f569e",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines decimalTailRel's zero-format case as the code sequence for 0db; it is a named result-format summary.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-bb0dd8b44a02de305b300de162887fd197bafc6ab3bffe93bdff08e62e6f569e",
      "start_line": 28,
      "text": "  rule decimalTailRel(N, TAIL)\n    => TAIL ==K iCons(48, iCons(100, iCons(98, .IntSeq)))\n    requires N ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 34,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "288f1d1aa76e8c443e284a26c6a3ffaa6dc11746b856850011993c220b27b228",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines decimalTailRel for positive inputs by invoking the already defined binRel recurrence with the trailing db accumulator.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-288f1d1aa76e8c443e284a26c6a3ffaa6dc11746b856850011993c220b27b228",
      "start_line": 32,
      "text": "  rule decimalTailRel(N, TAIL)\n    => binRel(N, iCons(100, iCons(98, .IntSeq)), TAIL)\n    requires N >Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 37,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "b28ffaf5f18a64587bbe6d9f806d4536c273d62a4236f1341522cafaef664d27",
      "rationale": "This equation completes decimalTailRel's guarded sign partition by defining negative inputs as false; it is a totalization case for the mathematical summary.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-b28ffaf5f18a64587bbe6d9f806d4536c273d62a4236f1341522cafaef664d27",
      "start_line": 36,
      "text": "  rule decimalTailRel(N, _TAIL) => false\n    requires N <Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 42,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "7c2e6fd20be28dd4a2b6f16a4389ef39d505f39f3f321b7eab857f76d1bf7526",
      "rationale": "This structural equation defines decimalResultRel for sequences with the required leading db codes by delegating the remaining sequence to decimalTailRel.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7c2e6fd20be28dd4a2b6f16a4389ef39d505f39f3f321b7eab857f76d1bf7526",
      "start_line": 41,
      "text": "  rule decimalResultRel(N, iCons(100, iCons(98, TAIL)))\n    => decimalTailRel(N, TAIL)"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [
        "owise"
      ],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 44,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "c6ae0b2b0ab8b9dfc28262926c22380fb803f9275d4e040bba7d777a9d8c61d9",
      "rationale": "This owise equation defines decimalResultRel as false for every sequence not handled by its leading-db structural case, making the named summary total.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-c6ae0b2b0ab8b9dfc28262926c22380fb803f9275d4e040bba7d777a9d8c61d9",
      "start_line": 44,
      "text": "  rule decimalResultRel(_N, _CODES) => false [owise]"
    }
  ],
